  "content": {
    "problemStatement": "There are NNN events (numbered from 111 to NNN) and MMM contestants (numbered from 111 to MMM). For each event iii, contestant jjj receives a predetermined number of points Ai,jA_{i, j}Ai,j​.\n\nA subset of these events will be selected, and the final score of contestant jjj, denoted sjs_jsj​, will be the sum of their points for each event selected.\n\nFormally, if SSS denotes the set of events chosen, then sj=∑x∈SAx,j\\displaystyle s_j = \\sum_{x \\in S} A_{x, j}sj​=x∈S∑​Ax,j​ for each 1≤j≤M1 \\leq j \\leq M1≤j≤M. If SSS is empty, we define sj=0s_j = 0sj​=0 for each jjj.\n\nThe differentiation of the final scoreboard is equal to\n\nmax⁡i=1M(∑j=1M∣sj−si∣)\\max_{i=1}^M \\left(\\sum_{j=1}^M |s_j - s_i|\\right)i=1maxM​(j=1∑M​∣sj​−si​∣)Find the maximum possible differentiation over all subsets of events.\n\n\nInput Format\n\nThe first line of input will contain a single integer TTT, denoting the number of test cases.\nEach test case consists of several lines.\n\nThe first line of each test case contains two space-separated integers NNN and MMM — the number of events and contestants, respectively.\nThe next NNN lines describe the events. The iii-th of these NNN lines contains MMM space-separated integers Ai,1,Ai,2,…,Ai,MA_{i, 1}, A_{i, 2}, \\ldots, A_{i, M}Ai,1​,Ai,2​,…,Ai,M​ — the jjj-th of which describes the number of points the jjj-th contestant earns for event iii.\n\n\n\n\nOutput Format\nFor each test case, output on a new line the maximum differentiation over all subsets of events.",
    "constraints": [
      "1≤T≤1001 \\leq T \\leq 1001≤T≤100",
      "1≤N≤1051 \\leq N \\leq 10^51≤N≤105",
      "1≤M≤1051 \\leq M \\leq 10^51≤M≤105",
      "0≤Ai,j≤1050 \\leq A_{i, j} \\leq 10^50≤Ai,j​≤105",
      "The sum of N⋅MN\\cdot MN⋅M over all test cases won't exceed 10510^5105."
    ],
